Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:16:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] Read the ERA5 files of the examples; terrain-shadow
 check on the sub-steps

- get_era5() reads earlier netCDF files (PLEV_*.nc, SURF_*.nc) that cover a
  larger box or more pressure levels than the request: the nodes and levels of
  the request are selected. The files shipped with the Finse example (box
  59.75-61.25 N, 14 levels) were not used, and get_era5() asked the CDS.
- The physics check direct_in_terrain_shadow tests the sun at the sub-steps of
  the accumulation window, as the downscaling shades the direct beam, when the
  checks compute the solar geometry. Testing the window centres of the previous,
  current and next steps flagged the sun passing between two ridges as an error
  (Finse, Oct-Dec 2018: 28 time steps). direct_with_sun_down uses the sub-steps
  too. With a saved ds_solar, the former approximation is kept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
